<h2>1. ElevenLabs — Best for Producing Narration</h2>
<p>ElevenLabs is the benchmark for generated speech. The current flagship model is Eleven v4, marketed as the most emotive text-to-speech model the company has shipped; Flash v2.5 targets roughly 75ms latency for conversational use. The pricing page lists 74 languages across all paid tiers, and the free tier still includes 10,000 credits a month — enough to finish a short pilot and judge the voice quality yourself.</p>
<p>The billing unit is characters: one character of text costs about one credit. That makes the per-minute maths simple and slightly uncomfortable — a minute of speech is roughly 1,000 characters, so Starter's 30,000 credits is about 30 minutes a month and Creator's 121,000 credits about two hours. Professional Voice Cloning (from around 30 minutes of reference audio) requires a paid plan; instant cloning works from a short clean sample.</p>

