<h2>2. Descript — Best When the Voice Lives Inside a Video Edit</h2>
<p>Descript is a video and podcast editor whose voice features are part of the edit rather than a separate app: Overdub patches a mis-spoken line by typing the correction, Studio Sound cleans room noise, and 25+ stock AI speakers plus custom voice clones cover narration inside the same timeline. If you already edit talking-head video, adding a separate TTS subscription is usually redundant.</p>
<p>Free covers 60 media minutes a month at 720p; Hobbyist is $16/month billed annually ($24 monthly) for 600 minutes, 1080p and the fuller AI toolset; Creator is $24/month annual ($35 monthly) for 1,800 minutes and 4K. Caption translation covers 61 languages and audio dubbing 30, which makes it a serviceable localisation tool as well.</p>

