<h2>How to Choose</h2>
<p><strong>If you need a voice file for video:</strong> ElevenLabs. Start on the free 10,000 credits, then move to Starter only if 30 minutes a month is enough — otherwise Creator.</p>
<p><strong>If you already edit in a timeline:</strong> Descript, because paying for a second tool only makes sense if you need voice quality Descript cannot reach.</p>
<p><strong>If you want to listen rather than produce:</strong> Speechify Premium, and ignore every TTS comparison that ranks it against ElevenLabs — they solve different problems.</p>
<p><strong>If your usage is sporadic:</strong> Murf's non-expiring API credit avoids the subscription you will forget to cancel.</p>
<p><strong>If you make music:</strong> Kits AI, and read the download-minute limits carefully — conversion minutes are the cheap part.</p>

<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<h3>What is the best AI voice generator overall?</h3>
<p>For producing audio, ElevenLabs: 74 languages, cloning from a short sample, 10,000 free credits a month, Starter at $6/month and Creator at $22/month. For listening to text instead of producing it, Speechify is the better buy.</p>

<h3>How much does AI voice generation cost per minute?</h3>
<p>On ElevenLabs one credit ≈ one character, so a minute of speech (≈1,000 characters) costs about 1,000 credits — roughly $0.20/minute on Starter and $0.17 on Pro. Murf publishes $0.01 per 1,000 characters on Falcon 2.1 and $0.03 on Gen2, roughly $0.15-0.45 per minute depending on model.</p>

<h3>Can I clone my own voice?</h3>
<p>Yes. ElevenLabs clones instantly from a one-to-two-minute clean sample and offers Professional Voice Cloning from about 30 minutes of audio on paid plans. Kits AI includes both clone types from $10/month. Cloning a third party's voice requires their explicit consent on every one of these platforms.</p>

<h3>Is Speechify a voice generator?</h3>
<p>It is primarily a reader — text-to-speech for articles, PDFs and documents — with 1,000+ voices and 60+ languages on Premium. Speechify Studio is the separate product for producing voiceover and dubbing.</p>

<h3>Is PlayHT still available?</h3>
<p>No. PlayHT was acquired by Meta in July 2025 and shut down on 31 December 2025. Any 2026 list that still recommends it has not been updated.</p>

<h2>How We Evaluate</h2>
<p>Tools are compared on published pricing, vendor-stated credit rates and documented capabilities. We do not present lab-style test results we did not produce.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope:</strong> Producing speech, cloning voices, dubbing video, and reading text aloud — treated as four separate jobs.</li>
<li><strong>Method:</strong> Official pricing pages, API rate cards and documentation, verified on the date shown above.</li>
<li><strong>Criteria:</strong> Cost per finished minute, language coverage, cloning requirements, free-tier usefulness, and measurable licensing limits.</li>
<li><strong>Corrections:</strong> Voice pricing changes often. Email admin@aizest.net with a source and we will update the page.</li>
</ul>

